  "items": [
    {
      "external_id": "C11-PHY-CH2-2.4-DERIVATION-OF-SECOND-EQUATION-OF-MOTION",
      "chapter": "pk-punjab/xi/physics/c11-phy/ch2",
      "topic": "pk-punjab/xi/physics/c11-phy/ch2/u-derivation-of-second-equation-of-motion",
      "title": "Derivation of Second Equation of Motion",
      "language": "en",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "e2c5c034-041b-5340-9823-5e3c8c88a07c",
          "pdf_from": 28,
          "pdf_to": 28,
          "note": "Derivation of Second Equation of Motion: a main subheading of 2.4 Equations of motion, its own page (owner 2026-11-04); PDF 28-28."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Suppose a body is moving with uniform acceleration a along a straight line with an initial velocity vi, which become vf after time interval t. Let it covers a distance S in a particular direction during time t, then using the definition of velocity as rate of change of displacement, we can write"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\text{Velocity} = \\text{Displacement}/\\text{Time}",
            "text_alt": "Velocity = Displacement/Time"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\text{or}\\quad \\text{Displacement} = \\text{Velocity} \\times \\text{time}",
            "text_alt": "or Displacement = Velocity × time"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "If velocity of the body is not constant, we can use average velocity instead of velocity. Thus"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\text{Displacement} = \\text{Average velocity} \\times \\text{Time}",
            "text_alt": "Displacement = Average velocity × Time"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\text{Displacement} = \\frac{(\\text{Final velocity} + \\text{Initial velocity})}{2} \\times \\text{Time}",
            "text_alt": "Displacement = (Final velocity + Initial velocity)/2 × Time"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "S = \\frac{(v_i + v_f)}{2} \\times t",
            "text_alt": "S = (vi + vf)/2 × t"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\text{Using first equation of motion,}\\quad S = \\frac{(v_i + v_i + at)}{2} \\times t",
            "text_alt": "Using first equation of motion, S = (vi + vi + at)/2 × t"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "S = \\frac{(2v_i + at)}{2} \\times t",
            "text_alt": "S = (2vi + at)/2 × t"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "2S = 2v_it + at^2",
            "text_alt": "2S = 2vit + at²"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "S = v_it + \\frac{1}{2}at^2 \\tag{2.14}",
            "text_alt": "S = vit + ½at²   (2.14)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "This is the second equation of motion."
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
